infographic compare-quadrant-quarter-simple-card
data
  title Replication modes: durability of an ack vs write availability
  desc Two axes — does an acknowledged write survive a single-node crash, and do writes keep flowing when a replica is down
  compares
    - label Fully async — fast but lossy
      desc Low durability, high availability. Leader acks before shipping; a crash loses acknowledged writes. Fine for logs/metrics.
    - label Semi-sync — the production middle
      desc High durability, high availability. One sync follower (ack = on two nodes) + async rest; one slow replica can't stall writes.
    - label Fully sync — durable but fragile
      desc High durability, low availability. Survives N-1 losses, but any slow/down replica blocks every write.
    - label Leaderless R+W>N — available, conflict-prone
      desc High durability, high availability, but quorum adds latency and writes need app-level conflict resolution.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #10b981 #f59e0b #6366f1
